kill - send a signal to a process

SYNOPSIS
    kill [-s signal] [--] pid ...

DESCRIPTION
    Send TERM by default. Use a number or a name such as STOP, CONT or
    QUIT. Use -- before a negative PID when specifying a process group.

EXAMPLES
    kill -s STOP 42

SEE ALSO
    waitpid(2), sh(1)
